        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.083,
            0.744,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": "Repeat the activity by using an iron bar in place of one of the magnets. What do you observe this time? You will find that both the ends of the iron bar will be attracted by both the North and South poles of the magnet. From this activity, we find that a magnet can be identified by its property of repulsion."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.229,
            0.452,
            0.251
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 4.6: Let us experiment"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.26,
            0.531,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "Take a magnetic compass and a bar magnet."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.305,
            0.502,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": " Place the magnetic compass over a horizontal surface and wait for its needle to come to rest."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.285,
            0.764,
            0.376
          ],
          "content": "The compass needle is also a magnet. Will it show the same behaviour if a magnet is brought closer to it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.368,
            0.744,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "Now slowly bring North pole of the bar magnet close to the North pole of the compass needle as shown in Fig. 4.9a. Observe the compass needle carefully. What do you observe? Does the needle deflect? If yes, in which direction?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.75,
            0.301,
            0.918,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.488,
            0.743,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": " Now repeat the above step with the South pole of the bar magnet. Do you observe any difference this time?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
